  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lagos State Employment Trust (LSETF)- Nightingale&apos;s Medical Care Training Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the arrival of the novel coronavirus, USADF and LSETF collaborated to conduct a Request for Proposals focused on healthcare services, infection control and sanitation, and PPE production. Nightingale&apos;s Caregivers Academy is proposing to train 100 young Nigerians resident in Lagos. The company will provide trainings in elder health caregiving. The company plans to have the training in batches of 35, 35, and 30 persons over 40 days of coursework. The company believes that there is enough demand in the market to absorb most of trainees after the training program.</narrative>
  </description>
